# preimport-validator.properties -- put this file in the app's /config folder (Sonarr, Radarr; Sportarr: see the README)
# and restart the container. Without it, or without a Url, completed downloads are imported exactly as upstream does.
#
# Before importing a completed download the app asks this service whether it is ready:
#     POST <Url>/validate   {"path": "<the download's folder or file>", "tags": ["<tag>", ...]}
#     -> {"ready": true|false, "failed": true|false, "message": "..."}
# ready=true imports. ready=false waits and asks again on the next queue refresh. failed=true marks the download
# failed (blocklisted; removed from the download client if that client's Remove Failed Downloads is on).
# An error, a timeout (10 s) or an unreadable answer also waits: the import never proceeds on a missing answer.
#
# "tags" is every tag the series/movie (Sportarr: league) has, unfiltered, left out when there are none. The app does
# not know which of them names a Tdarr quality tier: the Tdarr service below decides, from its own TDARR_LIBRARY_MAP,
# which library to scan this download into (its default library when none of the tags is in the map).
#
# For the Tdarr service in this repository (bdelima/tdarr-download-validator):
Url=http://tdarr-download-validator:8080
